<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Quintus Lollius Urbicus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 2nd century</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Quintus Lollius Urbicus was a Roman general from Numidia in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a> who served as governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> from about 139 to 142 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antoninus-pius">Antoninus Pius</a>. He reoccupied southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> and built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antonine-wall">Antonine Wall</a> between the Forth and the Clyde, moving the frontier north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hadrians-wall">Hadrian's Wall</a>. He later became prefect of the city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/quintus-lollius-urbicus.jpg" alt="Quintus Lollius Urbicus" width="320" height="218" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:RIB_1276_Rochester.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
